1
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:08,886
Whiskers and the Missing Sun.

2
00:00:19,347 --> 00:00:24,022
It had rained all week, and the cats hadn't seen the sun even once.

3
00:00:24,222 --> 00:00:29,334
So Luna built a giant puzzle of the Greek island of Santorini.

4
00:00:29,534 --> 00:00:34,254
White houses, blue domes... and in Oia, everybody claps when the sun goes down!

5
00:00:39,584 --> 00:00:42,365
But look. The very last piece is missing. The sun!

6
00:00:42,565 --> 00:00:45,860
Don't look at me. I've been sitting right here all day.

7
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:56,322
Kalispera, little cats! I'm flying home to Santorini, where the sun always shines.

8
00:00:56,522 --> 00:00:58,026
Do they have fish there?

9
00:00:58,226 --> 00:01:02,373
Grilled octopus! Tomato fritters! Hop in my beak, there's plenty of room.

10
00:01:08,730 --> 00:01:09,771
Wait for me!

11
00:01:13,049 --> 00:01:18,085
So off they flew, tucked inside a pelican's beak, far away to the south.

12
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:30,621
It smells like a fish shop in here. I love it.

13
00:01:38,004 --> 00:01:44,402
At sunrise they saw it: a ring of cliffs in the deep blue sea, around a sleeping volcano.

14
00:01:44,602 --> 00:01:47,882
The houses look like sugar cubes, sprinkled on the cliffs!

15
00:01:58,343 --> 00:02:02,430
Welcome to the old port! First, breakfast at my cousin's taverna.

16
00:02:02,630 --> 00:02:08,184
There were tomato fritters, grilled octopus, and more octopus, hanging up to dry.

17
00:02:12,489 --> 00:02:15,334
That big one is mine. Nobody move.

18
00:02:24,256 --> 00:02:27,436
I'm fine! I'm just... washing the octopus.

19
00:02:27,636 --> 00:02:31,103
Whiskers! The sunset is in Oia, at the top of the island.

20
00:02:31,303 --> 00:02:34,942
Then up the steps you go. Five hundred and eighty-eight of them!

21
00:02:35,142 --> 00:02:38,527
Five hundred? I'm a cat, not a mountain goat.

22
00:02:45,909 --> 00:02:50,412
Need a ride, little ones? I'm Fasolaki. I carry everybody up the steps.

23
00:02:50,612 --> 00:02:53,150
Finally! Someone who understands me.

24
00:03:05,664 --> 00:03:08,615
This is the life! A little faster, please!

25
00:03:13,945 --> 00:03:15,872
Whiskers, listen. She's puffing.

26
00:03:16,072 --> 00:03:19,279
Don't worry. I've climbed these steps every day of my life.

27
00:03:19,479 --> 00:03:24,979
I only wish I could see the Oia sunset, just once. But by evening, I'm too tired.

28
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:34,546
Then today, nobody carries me. I carry you. Well... your bags.

29
00:03:34,746 --> 00:03:36,508
And we'll all walk to Oia together!

30
00:03:39,787 --> 00:03:45,436
So the friends walked the cliff path together, past windmills, blue domes and ringing bells.

31
00:03:55,897 --> 00:03:58,674
Heavy bags. Little legs. Very far.

32
00:03:58,874 --> 00:04:01,625
I'll help! A mouse can carry a lot more than you think.

33
00:04:01,825 --> 00:04:04,623
You know, a heavy load is lighter when friends share it.

34
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:12,836
Hurry! The sun is getting low!

35
00:04:24,323 --> 00:04:27,976
In Oia, everyone waited on the rooftops and walls.

36
00:04:41,515 --> 00:04:43,827
Oh... It's even more beautiful than I dreamed.

37
00:04:44,027 --> 00:04:48,740
Worth every single step. Even the four hundred I complained about.

38
00:04:58,175 --> 00:05:00,021
Everybody's clapping for the sun!

39
00:05:00,221 --> 00:05:03,308
Bravo! And now, little cats, the night flight home.

40
00:05:13,769 --> 00:05:16,513
Back home, the rain had stopped at last.

41
00:05:16,713 --> 00:05:18,547
But our puzzle still has no sun.

42
00:05:23,877 --> 00:05:25,863
Whiskers! It's stuck on your bottom!

43
00:05:26,063 --> 00:05:28,698
I was keeping it warm. On purpose.

44
00:05:36,081 --> 00:05:41,461
Because any load feels lighter, and any road feels shorter, when friends share it.

